{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Pseudocode and Its Importance", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 12, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about pseudocode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe the development of software programming in simple spoken and written situations. Read and write information about designing principles in software programming", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history. Writes basic ideas on programming concepts and/or programming history.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Negative Imperatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>negative imperatives</strong> to give  instructions or commands about actions that you don't want other people to do.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Imperatives  are useful to express others what we expect them to do or <strong>not</strong> to do. When we use imperative sentences <strong>negative</strong> in the negative form, we have to start the command with <strong>do not</strong> or <strong>don't</strong>.   Structure: </br></br>  <center><strong> Do not (Don't) </strong>+ verb in base form+ complement + period (.) or exclamation sign (!)</center></br></br>  Here we have some examples: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\"> <li><strong>Do not</strong> use long statements, make it simple! </br> <li><strong>Don't</strong> use long statements, make it simple.</span> <br><br>At the end of the  sentence, we need to add a period (.) or an exclamation sign (!); that depends on the communicative intention of the command. </br></br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "But, make no mistake, do not take the term \u201cpseudocode\u201d as a programming language, it is instead a simpler way to write code before using an actual language. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "First, do not forget that the instructions used in pseudocode need to be universal. Do not use any language specific-commands since this format is not used in compilation or execution.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Basic Guidelines to Use Pseudocode", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Pseudocode is a simple method to write code statements when mapping out programs. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>The main objective of using pseudocodes is to make programming easier for software developers since most of the times programs can be difficult and hard to elaborate.</p> <p>The first step to using pseudocodes is to write what you need the program to show in English. This helps you organize your ideas. Make sure you use short statements. And do not include language-specific commands because pseudocodes must be universal. The second step is to divide the tasks that your program will perform by lines. The idea is not to overburden the processes with confusing information.</p> <p>The next step is to make sure that important words are capitalized, so you will be able to recognize the main tasks in each instruction. Finally, make sure you indent statements in a loop, so you can see how the program flows.</p>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pseudocode", "type": "name"}, {"content": "simple code that can be translated into any programming language", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One effective way to solve these matters is using pseudocode, which is a tool to ensure that all the information required in a program is included. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "short phrase ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sentence that has a small amount of words", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It has a friendly concept where you can write short phrases in English.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "capitalize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put the first letter of a word in upper case", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Third, do not capitalize all the words in your statements, you just need to capitalize keywords such as Start, Read, End, etc. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "indent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to provide an extra space at the beginning of a sentence ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Finally, do not forget to indent your statements, this eases the reading of the flow of your program. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "achieve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reach established goals", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In this way, this pre-coding method is really appealing for users since it offers a friendlier approach to achieve better programming results.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob12aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Find in the web examples of pseudocodes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read them and analyze the way they are written.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write those examples in a poster.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the poster to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe briefly their structure.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I find different examples of pseudocodes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I analyze the structure of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I show the pseudocodes to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe their structure.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can understand written information about the definition of pseudocode. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand written information about the importance of pseudocode. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can write pseudocode taking into consideration basic guidelines.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What programming methods do you know?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you have to use any specific programming language when using these methods? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Using Simple Programming!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id