{"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 12, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n1le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<strong>Jack:</strong> Thank you all for coming to our convention. Today's presentation is about pseudocode and its importance to our system engineering field. The information that I show you here is a case study which defines this concept as a tool to create programs in an easy way. Do not confuse this term with a programming language, it is more like a source of statements that helps us obtain the expected results in our program.</br><p>One effective way to solve these matters is using pseudocode, which is a tool to ensure that all the information required in a program is included. But, make no mistake, do not take the term &ldquo;pseudocode&rdquo; as a programming language, it is instead a simpler way to write code before using an actual language. In this way, this pre-coding method is really appealing for users since it offers a friendlier approach to achieve better programming results.</p>", "image": "enpe7n1le01ob12re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "28000", "text": "In this case, Professor Smith explains in his written document the importance of pseudocode. He says that programming can be a difficult task and that we usually use flowcharts to map out programs. However, flowcharts are not easy to modify, and they don't display all parts of a program. Pseudocode is important because it is more appealing for users since it has a friendly concept where you can write short phrases in English that later on can be translated into any language thanks to pseudocode. Don't complicate yourselves with difficult long statements, sometimes this makes things difficult and confusing. </br>", "image": "enpe7n1le01ob12re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "74000", "text": "To conclude the presentation, we need to understand the steps of a basic guideline to write pseudocode; so, later on, we start practicing. As I mention before, the first thing to do is to organize our ideas into short statements. In that way, it will be clear for us what we want to achieve. Don't forget using short phrases to write code for programs. The next step is to select some important words and capitalize them.  So, we let the program know what we want to show. Do not capitalize everything; you need to identify the most relevant tasks for your program. Finally, we just need to indent the statements and make sure they are in shown in a loop. </br></br>Now that we review this information, it's time to practice.", "image": "enpe7n1le01ob12re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n1le01ob12re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "video", "title": "", "id": 5, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "image": "", "id": 0}], "video_src": "enpe7n1le01ob12re5vsc01"}, "type": "video"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}